<title>FRANCE: Arianespace signs PanAmSat satellite launch deal.</title>
<headline>Arianespace signs PanAmSat satellite launch deal.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>European rocket consortium Arianespace said on Thursday that it has signed an agreement with PanAmSat Corp to launch a satellite in early 1999.</p>
<p>The launch is part of a previously signed multi-launch accord between the two companies and will use an Ariane rocket from the Guiana Space Centre in Kourou, South America, Arianespace said in a statement released at the Paris air show.</p>
<p>PanAmSat will deploy a high-power HS 702 satellite built by Hughes Spacce and Communications Co. No financial details were given.</p>
</text>
